                <pb facs="0592" n="468" xml:id="pg468"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.48B/39: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Woods</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-09-04"><hi rendition="#italic">September 4,
                        1923</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received September 8—12:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>This disaster without precedent in history, one-half million dead, several
                    million destitute and homeless, there is utter lack every necessity. President
                    of the United States should issue an appeal at once to the American people
                    relief along lines mentioned in my previous telegrams.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Woods</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
